>=20


This says "Please be a giving book about me" =C2=A0You want {pe'u ko dunda =
le=20
cukta mi}, if you have a patiuclar book in mind or {pe'u ko dunda lo cukta=
=20
mi} for a book, whatever comes to hand.



> ko jinru
>=20



OK (we will not at this point get fussy about what the child is to immerse=
=20
himself in and what he is to do in it, though given a six-year-old's=20
jesuitical strain, {ko lumci vo'a} might be safer)



> pe=E2=80=99u ko jgari mi
>=20



On the same ground, watch out for clutching and choking.



>=20
> ko gasnu vorme ganlo=20
>=20


This gets complex. {gasnu} object is an event description , {lenu...}, in=20
this case that the door (a specific one, I assume) is closed: le vorme cu=20
ganlo ({cu} to mark the beginning of the selbri -- or the end of the sumti)=
.=20
=C2=A0So the whole comes to=20
{ko gasnu lenu le vorme cu ganlo} =C2=A0(The original said --whatever it ma=
y mean=20
-- "Be agent doorly shut")





>=20
> xu skule pluka
>=20


xu le ckule cu pluka (do) (We skip over the fact that {pluka} expects an=20
event description in the first place, so the question is "really" about som=
e=20
event involving the school and so should have teh subject-rasing {tu'a} in=
=20
front of it. =C2=A0don't worry about that yet) =C2=A0The original is "Is it=
 a scholarly=20
pleasure?" =C2=A0





>=20
> lumci ledo fe xance
>=20


ko lumci ledo xance (the {fe} would go before {ledo} but is unneeded since=
=20
the sumti is in the right place)




> ko cliva klaji
> get out of the street
>=20


ko cliva le klaji (seems more of an abandonment, but I can't think of a=20
better word)





> pe=E2=80=99u ko zutse ledo stizu
> sit in your chair
>=20


Yup.



> ko smaji
> be quiet
>=20


And yup again.

A really nice start!

           
